  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Norec, FK Norway, personnell exchange</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tanzania, Uganda. Innovate4FoodSecurity, a joint effort between StartHub Africa in Uganda and Ignite Africa Ltd trading as Ennovate Ventures in Tanzania aims at creating sustainable entrepreneurial ventures that can mitigate the effects of climate change on food security. The project will increase youth participation in income generating activities within the agricultural value chain through entrepreneurship support programs. Project activities will target 504 enthusiastic young people at different intervention levels per round which resulted in two years (2 rounds) total of 1008 young people empowered in Uganda and Tanzania. Through this project young people would  be able to enhance their capacities which will enable them to create opportunities in the agricultural value chain which will go beyond on just having employments.</narrative>
  </description>
